# Line-ending policy for the digest-pinned Hermes audit surface.
#
# The Spec 026-034 audit chain pins file bytes with SHA-256: reviewed-artifact
# manifests, source-bundle manifests, predecessor digests, and the pinned
# upstream bundle are all hashed verbatim. This repository is authored on
# Windows (CRLF) while `core.autocrlf=input` stores LF, so a clone that checks
# out LF -- exactly the WSL/Linux host the Hermes runbook requires -- would
# change those bytes and invalidate every digest. The failure surfaces as
# BLOCKED_SOURCE_GRAPH and dozens of audit-test failures that look like a
# security regression rather than an end-of-line conversion.
#
# Keep every digest-pinned surface byte-identical on all platforms.
#
# Every rule below sets the same attribute, so the grouping and the ordering
# inside each group exist only to make the list reviewable: there are no
# overriding later rules, and no path depends on where it appears. Adding a
# hashed path to the "wrong" group still pins it; leaving one out silently
# un-pins a file the audit chain hashes, which is the failure this file exists
# to prevent. When a new Hermes or spec-03x surface lands, add it to the group
# it belongs to and keep that group sorted.

# The audit chain itself: spec packages 026-034.
specs/026-hermes-mcp-integration/** -text
specs/027-hermes-skill-routing-contracts/** -text
specs/028-hermes-runtime-skill-routing-observation/** -text
specs/029-hermes-blocked-tool-attempt-runtime-smoke/** -text
specs/030-hermes-g1r-offline-remediation/** -text
specs/031-hermes-g2-credentialless-activation-gate/** -text
specs/032-hermes-g2-offline-attempt-executor/** -text
specs/033-hermes-v019-pinned-source-loader-audit/** -text
specs/034-hermes-v019-pinned-startup-source-graph/** -text

# Sidecar deployment surface (Dockerfile, compose, runbook, helper shell).
deploy/** -text

# Runtime modules the chain hashes.
src/podcast_ingest_core/hermes_*.py -text

# Tests: the Hermes suites, the transport suite they share, and the
# non-test_ helper module that spec034's final acceptance imports.
tests/spec034_final_c6_support.py -text
tests/test_hermes_*.py -text
tests/test_mcp_http_transport.py -text
tests/test_spec_02[6-9]*.py -text
tests/test_spec_03*.py -text

# Scripts: the offline entry points and the servers they drive. Both
# `spec_03`/`spec03` spellings are listed on purpose -- the chain shipped
# under both naming conventions.
scripts/*hermes*.py -text
scripts/*spec_03*.py -text
scripts/build_hermes_sidecar.sh -text
scripts/export_spec029_tool_descriptor_snapshot.py -text
scripts/run_mcp_deny_interposer.py -text
scripts/run_mcp_http_server.py -text
scripts/spec03*.py -text
